# Koro — User-Only Website Development Prompt

Build the Koro website on top of the existing **Spring Boot + MongoDB backend with JWT authentication**.

This frontend is **ONLY for normal users and public visitors**.

## Important Scope

Do NOT build:

* Admin dashboard
* Admin pages
* Admin navigation
* Admin settings
* User management
* Language management
* Concept management
* Translation management
* Submission moderation
* Reviewer dashboard
* Admin analytics
* Admin activity logs

The backend may already contain admin/reviewer APIs, but **do not expose or implement them in this website**.

The website should focus entirely on the public language-discovery experience and normal authenticated user experience.

---

# 1. Main Product Principle

The most important rule is:

> **Explore first. Login only when you want to save or use personal features.**

A visitor must be able to use the public website without creating an account.

### Without Login

Users can:

* Explore Koro
* Browse languages
* Search languages
* Browse dictionary
* Search concepts
* View translations
* View pronunciation
* View language information
* Read about Koro

### Login Required

Users must log in to:

* Save words
* Create books
* Add words to books
* Manage books
* Export books
* Scan objects
* View scan history
* Submit translations
* View personal submissions
* View personal activity
* Manage profile/settings

