# 32. Final Requirement

Build a **user-only Koro website**.

The website must have two simple experiences:

### Public

```text
Explore → Search → Learn
```

### Authenticated

```text
Learn → Save → Organize → Practice → Contribute
```

Do not build any admin or reviewer UI.

Do not force visitors to log in.

The primary purpose of the website is to make Koro's language content **easy to discover and use**, while giving registered users additional personal features such as books, saved words, scanning, submissions, activity, and PDF export.

The most important UX principle is:

> **Anyone can come to Koro and start learning immediately. Create an account only when you want to make Koro personal.**
